<p>Unfortunately this is probably a bit too big for us to tackle for the EUTS. Internally, we used 3DSMax and exported animations using some scripts that we weren't able to release for legal reasons. We've released the schema for animation and model mesh files (see <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/ANI" title="ANI">ANI</a>), so hopefully at some point soon community members will write the necessary conversion programs much as was done with model meshes and you'll be able to use the same sort of workflow yourself. Links to such tools should go here when they appear: <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/3rd%20party%20extensions" title="3rd party extensions">3rd party extensions</a>. I'll leave this feature request here anyway, though, just in case. <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20BryanDerksen" title="User:BryanDerksen">BryanDerksen</a> 17:25, 19 January 2010 (UTC)
</p>
